               <item>
                <widget class="QLabel" name="references_label">
                 <property name="font">
                  <font>
                   <pointsize>10</pointsize>
                  </font>
                 </property>
                 <property name="text">
                  <string>[1] Vallat, R., &amp;amp; Walker, M. P. (2021). An open-source, high-performance tool for automated sleep staging. &lt;i&gt;eLife&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;10&lt;/i&gt;, Article e70092. &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.70092"&gt;https://doi.org/10.7554/eLife.70092&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;[2] Yetton, B. D., Niknazar, M., Duggan, K. A., McDevitt, E. A., Whitehurst, L. N., Sattari, N., &amp;amp; Mednick, S. C. (2016). Automatic detection of rapid eye movements (REMs): A machine learning approach. &lt;i&gt;Journal of Neuroscience Methods&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;259&lt;/i&gt;, 72–82. &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jneumeth.2015.11.015"&gt;https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jneumeth.2015.11.015&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;[3] Agarwal, R., Takeuchi, T., Laroche, S., &amp;amp; Gotman, J. (2005). Detection of rapid-eye movements in sleep studies. &lt;i&gt;IEEE Transactions on Biomedical Engineering&lt;/i&gt;, &lt;i&gt;52&lt;/i&gt;(8), 1390–1396. &lt;a href="https://doi.org/10.1109/TBME.2005.851512"&gt;https://doi.org/10.1109/TBME.2005.851512&lt;/a&gt;</string>
                 </property>
